status: accept
exit: 42
note: |
  Rebinding a place variable to a fresh instance, then reading a field.
  Content-addressing makes p.x = e (in-place field mutation) impossible, so the
  ONLY coherent "mutation" is the handle swap: p = new Pt {...} builds a new slot
  and points the cell at the new handle. This exercises that a place stays
  first-class through the mutable (cell-promoted) path: the section handle survives
  the round-trip through the f64 cell and p.x projects the new value. Fixed
  2026-07-02 (before, reading a field after = CRASHED emit_mlir: the promoted cell
  lost the section type).
